I walk in the main hall of the museum.
It is very quiet here.
It is raining outside, but inside it is completely dry.
Many old objects are displayed in the hall.
I stop near a glass case.
There are old clay pots in this case.
Those pots are very beautiful.
I read the information plaque in front of it.
These pots are from many centuries ago.
Hundreds of years ago, people used these pots every day.
I go to the next case.
There are some old coins there.
This is a copper coin.
And that is a silver coin.
Many years ago, people bought things with these coins.
I feel very amazed.
Life so many years ago was also somewhat like today's.
They used these simple objects in their daily lives.
Those days of theirs were just like my days.
